2026-10-23T10:15:21.2542213Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons[0m
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2544250Z    [0m[36m┌─[0m /home/runner/work/rust-agentic-foundations/rust-agentic-foundations/fuzz/Cargo.lock:20:1
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2545091Z    [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2545757Z [0m[36m20[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mctutils 0.4.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2547567Z    [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2548756Z    [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2549358Z    [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2550377Z    [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2551373Z    [0m[36m├[0m ## Summary
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2551888Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2560388Z      The `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2561073Z      integer size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2561711Z      therefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2562278Z      that's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2562642Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2563045Z      In releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2563685Z      include a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2564275Z      release and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2564714Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2565142Z      Additionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2565831Z      intended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2566465Z      This has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2566959Z      for such targets.
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2567217Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2567439Z      ## Impact
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2567682Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2568061Z      Branch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2569001Z      covert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2569508Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2569727Z      ## Resolution
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2569965Z      
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2570327Z      This has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2570957Z      which in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2571602Z      this resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2572612Z      of target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2573121Z      automatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2573803Z    [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569
2026-10-23T10:15:21.2574550Z    [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=0.4.4 (try `cargo update -p ctutils`)
